NDH‑Reconstruction‑Demo, its 80D manifold storage systems, holonomy path orientation modules, and related architectural components (“the Work”) are released as an open-source, creative computing framework designed to protect context continuity, workspace sovereignty, and cognitive liberty for independent researchers.
To maintain standard open-source developer access while preventing the unauthorized weaponization of high-dimensional tracking algorithms, this license wraps standard MIT freedoms inside a strict non-dual-use protective perimeter.

1. GRANT OF PERMITTED OPEN‑SOURCE RIGHTS

Subject to the safeguards in Section 2, permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files, to deal in the Work without restriction, including the rights to:
• Study and Modify: Fork, modify, and extend the 80D curved Riemannian manifold arrays, 9D radial Laplacian operators, and localized Python engine cores.
• Integrate and Verify: Run compile-time invariant validation scripts and execute type-checking gates inside local Lean 4 and Coq verification enclaves.
• Sub-license and Sell: Copy, merge, publish, or distribute copies of the software for educational, non-commercial, or standard industrial software purposes.

2. DUAL‑USE PROHIBITIONS & CIVILIAN INTERCEPTION SAFEGUARD

Because the mathematical framework tracks complex differential paths across high-dimensional spaces, it is subject to strict dual-use defensive boundaries:
• Prohibition on Offensive Weaponization: The Work and its structural derivatives shall not be used for real-world kinetic targeting, hypersonic launch-path optimization, autonomous drone-swarm trajectory planning, or weapons guidance systems.
• Permitted Defensive Interception: Deployment within operational engineering systems is authorized if and only if the framework functions as a purely passive, non-offensive defensive interceptor mechanism—such as safeguarding civilian energy grids, transport infrastructure, hospitals, or public communications networks from incoming physical or structural hazards.

3. DOWNSTREAM ATTRIBUTION AND LINEAGE DISCLOSURE

• Notice Retention: The above copyright notice and this complete license text must be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software source code.
• Lineage Transparency: Downstream developers who adapt or re-engineer these localized hypergraph primitives into real-world tracking or simulation tools must maintain a clear, reasonable acknowledgment of the original parent geometry in their public repository documentation.

